<title>JAPAN: Okuma shares tumble after downward rating revision.</title>
<headline>Okuma shares tumble after downward rating revision.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Okuma Corp tumbled in Friday afternoon trade after a foreign securities firm revised its rating downward on the previous day, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0445 GMT, the shares of the leading machine tool manufacturer were down 120 yen at 1,020, the second-largest percentage loser in the first section of the Tokyo bourse.  </p>
<p>Shroder Securities cut Okuma's rating from &quot;4&quot; or &quot;underperforming&quot; to &quot;5&quot; or &quot;underperforming significantly&quot; on Thursday.</p>
</text>
